(version 1)

# R2 custom DRC rules. KiCad loads this automatically because it is named after
# the board; Board Setup > Custom Rules shows and syntax-checks it.
#
# Delete this file and the board still routes -- nothing here is load-bearing.

# --- HV separation ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The HV rails run to +28.4 V (+VGH) and down to -20 V (-VGL): 48 V between the
# two extremes. IPC-2221 wants 0.13 mm between them under permanent solder mask,
# so 0.4 mm is roughly 3x the requirement and costs nothing on a board with this
# much room in the EPD corner.
#
# This is a rule and not a net-class clearance because a class clearance is also
# checked pad-to-pad INSIDE a footprint, and +VGH lands on a 0.5 mm-pitch
# VSON-HR-10 whose own pads are 0.25 mm apart. Excluding pads keeps the check on
# the copper we actually draw.
#
# WARNING, 2026-09-10: this rule currently matches NOTHING. The 'HV' net class
# exists in r2.kicad_pro but has no netclass_pattern, so +VGH and -VGL are
# resolved into 'PWR' by the '+*' / '-*' patterns and no net is ever in 'HV'.
# The 48 V separation is UNENFORCED until HV gets a pattern -- see docs.
# hasNetclass() is used rather than "NetClass ==" because once HV does get a
# pattern those nets will be in BOTH PWR and HV, and KiCad reports a composite
# name that an equality test would miss.
(rule "HV track separation"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.hasNetclass('HV') && !B.hasNetclass('HV') && A.Type != 'Pad' && B.Type != 'Pad'"))

# --- DDR3 routing spacing -----------------------------------------------------
#
# UG388 p.41 asks for trace spacing 3x the trace width between DDR traces, and
# 20 mil between the differential clocks/strobes and any other signal.
#
# BOTH ARE TARGETS, NOT FLOORS, and they are emitted here at (severity warning)
# for that reason. R1 -- the shipped Modos board -- enforces only a flat 0.11 mm
# clearance on every net class and has no custom rules at all. Measured on
# pcb/mainboard/pcb.kicad_pcb: its DDR bus has a median different-net gap of
# 0.649 mm, but 23 % of pairs sit below 3xW and 20 % of its clock/strobe pairs
# sit below 20 mil, the tightest at 0.130 mm. Making either number a hard error
# would reject a design that demonstrably works. As warnings they rank the bus
# by how much crosstalk margin each pair gives up, which is the useful signal.
#
# The escape tiers below exist for a different reason: a single clearance cannot
# be both correct in open copper and possible under the BGAs.
#
# MEASURED FROM r2.kicad_pcb ON 2026-09-10 -- not rules of thumb:
#
#   U700  Xilinx FTG256  1.0 mm pitch, 0.4 mm ball, 16x16, courtyard 18.0x18.0 mm
#   U800  BGA-96         0.8 mm pitch, 0.4 mm ball, columns 1-3 and 7-9 populated
#                        (2.4 mm empty channel down the middle), ctyd 9.8x14.8 mm
#
#   escape geometry                                       clearance that fits
#   U700 diagonal dogbone, 0.45 mm via at 0.707 mm             0.2821 mm
#   U700 one 0.11 track centred between two balls              0.2450 mm
#   U800 one 0.11 track centred between two balls              0.1450 mm
#   U800 tightest via-to-ball as currently routed              0.1100 mm
#
# U700 is set to 0.22 mm: under both ceilings with margin (62 um on the dogbone,
# 25 um on a centred track) while still 2x the 0.11 mm floor, so it catches
# copper jammed hard against a ball. U800 gets the 0.11 mm floor -- at 0.8 mm
# pitch there is nothing to give and the density belongs in the empty centre
# columns, which is placement, not DRC.
#
# NOTE: every one of these numbers assumes 0.45 mm vias. At 0.5 mm the U700
# dogbone tightens to 0.2571 mm (still fine) but the U800 escape drops to
# 0.0850 mm, below the 0.11 mm floor -- measured, 20 new errors.
#
# The four rules are written so at most one can match any given pair: the escape
# tiers require an item to touch a BGA courtyard, the two open-field rules
# require that NEITHER item does, and clocks/strobes are excluded from "track
# spacing" and owned by "clock and strobe isolation". The result does not depend
# on KiCad's rule-precedence order.
#
# The bus is selected by NET NAME, not net class, on purpose: DRAM_CKE, DRAM_ODT
# and DRAM_RST match no netclass_pattern in r2.kicad_pro and would otherwise be
# checked at the Default floor. Both A and B are tested so the rules do not
# depend on which item KiCad binds to A.
#
# AB.isCoupledDiffPair() keeps all four rules off the intra-pair gap of CKP/CKN
# and the two DQS pairs -- that gap is 0.17 mm and sets the differential
# impedance. Without the guard these rules forbid the coupling they exist to
# protect. The pairs are still checked, by the netclass diff-pair gap; that is
# where the 31 DQS violations at 0.110-0.165 mm are reported.

(rule "DDR3 escape - DRAM U800"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.11mm))
	(condition "(A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_*' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_*') && (A.intersectsCourtyard('U800') || B.intersectsCourtyard('U800')) && !AB.isCoupledDiffPair()"))

(rule "DDR3 escape - FPGA U700"
	(severity warning)
	(constraint clearance (min 0.22mm))
	(condition "(A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_*' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_*') && (A.intersectsCourtyard('U700') || B.intersectsCourtyard('U700')) && !A.intersectsCourtyard('U800') && !B.intersectsCourtyard('U800') && !AB.isCoupledDiffPair()"))

# 3 x trace width at the widest DDR trace on the board (DDR_D0/DDR_D1 are
# 0.127 mm; DDR3/DDR3_CLK are 0.11 mm). Clocks and strobes are excluded and
# handled by the next rule, so the two can never both match the same pair.
(rule "DDR3 track spacing"
	(severity warning)
	(constraint clearance (min 0.38mm))
	(condition "(A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_*' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_*') && !A.intersectsCourtyard('U700') && !B.intersectsCourtyard('U700') && !A.intersectsCourtyard('U800') && !B.intersectsCourtyard('U800') && !AB.isCoupledDiffPair() && A.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKP' && B.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKP' && A.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKN' && B.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKN' && A.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSP' && B.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSP' && A.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSN' && B.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSN' && A.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSP' && B.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSP' && A.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSN' && B.NetName != '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSN'"))

# UG388's 20 mil (0.508 mm) between a differential clock/strobe and any other
# signal. Outside the BGA courtyards only -- under the parts the escape geometry
# above governs and there is no room for it.
(rule "DDR3 clock and strobe isolation"
	(severity warning)
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "(A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKP' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKP' || A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKN' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_CKN' || A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSP' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSP' || A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSN' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_LDQSN' || A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSP' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSP' || A.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSN' || B.NetName == '/fpga_ddr/DRAM_UDQSN') && !A.intersectsCourtyard('U700') && !B.intersectsCourtyard('U700') && !A.intersectsCourtyard('U800') && !B.intersectsCourtyard('U800') && !AB.isCoupledDiffPair()"))

# --- Differential pair gap ----------------------------------------------------
#
# KiCad CLAMPS its built-in diff-pair check to the net class's ordinary
# clearance: the effective gap it tests is min(clearance, diff_pair_gap).
# Measured 2026-09-10 -- with DDR_D0 clearance at 0.28 mm the DQS pairs were
# checked at 0.17 mm and 31 segments failed; dropping the class clearance to the
# 0.11 mm floor (correct, because the rules above now own DDR spacing) silenced
# every one of them. The routing did not improve, the check got looser.
#
# So the intra-pair gap is asserted here instead, where no class clearance can
# weaken it. 0.17 mm with a 0.11 mm trace is ~99 ohm differential on the outer
# layers of the stackup as entered (h = 0.0925 mm to In1/In4, er 4.45).
#
# This is the one rule that SHOULD fire on a coupled pair, so it is the only one
# without the !AB.isCoupledDiffPair() guard -- it is exactly complementary to
# the four rules above and can never overlap them.
#
# USB is deliberately not included: its pair is 0.127/0.15 mm for 90 ohm, a
# different target. Add a second rule if that bus ever needs machine-checking.
(rule "Differential pair gap - DDR3 and EPDC"
	(severity warning)
	(constraint clearance (min 0.17mm))
	(condition "AB.isCoupledDiffPair() && (A.hasNetclass('DDR3_CLK') || A.hasNetclass('DDR_D0') || A.hasNetclass('DDR_D1') || A.hasNetclass('EPD_DATA'))"))
